## {{lb|en|military}} An area [[designated]] by [[boundary|boundaries]] within which a [[unit]] operates, and for which it is [[responsible]].
## {{lb|en|military}} One of the [[subdivision]]s of a [[coastal]] [[frontier]].
## {{lb|en|science fiction}} a [[fictional]] [[region]] of [[space]] designated for [[navigational]] or [[governance]] purposes.
## {{lb|en|micronationalism}} A [[community]] or [[subculture]] within the wider [[intermicronational]] community.
##* {{quote-web|en|date=24 April 2002|author=Kaiser Mors I|title=Imperial Decree #13: Sectors.|work=Imperial Republic of Shireroth forums|url=https://shireroth.org/forum/viewtopic.php?f=3&t=2448&p=33014|passage=Shireroth shall not recognize the use of '''Sectors'''{{sic}} as a micronational geographic or cultural subdivision. Nor shall it reside in any '''sector'''. Nor shall any duchy or territory be considered a part of ANY '''sector''' unless the Duchy or Territory expressly grants permision{{sic}} to be considered in such sector.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=12 December 2006|author=Sepatarist|title=CIS Disscussion|work=Micronational Cartography Society|url=https://micras.org/foruma/viewtopic.php?t=719|passage=I'll also provide a list of all active citizens, I understand that in the past this has been hard due to lack of updates of the necessary links but as someone said not so long ago the CIS '''sector''' is in more of a flux than other '''sectors''' - bar Lovely 😉}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=16 July 2009|author=claudre [Claudio de Castro]|title=Micronations with names of Macronations|work=List of Micronations Forum|url=https://listofmicronations.proboards.com/thread/194/micronations-names-macronations|passage=What are your opinions about this practice? Does it have a parallel outside the lusophone '''sector'''? Do you know of other stories other than YUGA? Does this mean micronationalism is changing? Is it good, bad, or irrelevant?}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=29 September 2012|author=H.A Gov|title=Re: University of Directus Releases Historic Study|work=Micras forums|url=https://hub.mn/forum/viewtopic.php?f=62&t=6245&p=73288|passage=Very interesting read. Love it, and very inspiring. I hope this will be good for nations. I am planning in a thing like this for the MicroWiki '''sector''', and MicroWikia '''sector''', so this is a good model.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=13 March 2021|title=Leaving For Greener Pastures|work=w:r/micronations|publisher=w:Reddit|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/micronations/comments/m4haox/leaving_for_greener_pastures/|passage=This is not a '''sector''' where micronations come together, it is a cesspool where the most toxic elements of micronationalism gather to engage in drama. I plan on having much stricter rules than this '''sector''' and several people to report abuse or immature activity to, rather than just the shoddy rules and rule enforcement and one semi-active admin here.}}
# {{lb|en|geometry}} Part of a [[circle]], extending to the [[center]]; [[circular sector]].
# {{lb|en|computer hardware}} A fixed-sized unit (traditionally 512 bytes) of sequential data stored on a [[track]] of a digital medium.
#: {{cot|en|block}}
# {{lb|en|calculation}} An instrument consisting of two rulers of equal length joined by a hinge.
# A field of [[economic]] [[activity]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-28|author=w:Joris Luyendijk
|volume=189|issue=3|page=21|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/joris-luyendijk-banking-blog/2013/jun/19/banking-britain-beyond-control Our banks are out of control]
|passage=Seeing the British establishment struggle with the financial '''sector''' is like watching an alcoholic who still resists the idea that something drastic needs to happen for him to turn his life around. Until 2008 there was denial over what finance had become. When a series of bank failures made this impossible, there was widespread anger, leading to the public humiliation of symbolic figures.}}
#: {{ux|en|public '''sector'''; private '''sector'''}}
